From f3e3bb1268f7a6bc4f10779cb91f02a7398604e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Null-H3x <null-h3x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:27:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] eyestat runner: always-on readable run_summary.txt for
 review

The runner only wrote bruteforce_results.txt when something cleared
threshold, so a clean multi-day null produced no readable artifact -- you
ended a 7-day run with a .tsv.gz of raw attempts and nothing to review.

Adds write_run_summary(): emits run_summary.txt unconditionally at end of
run AND every --summary-every completed units (default 25), so a killed
long run still leaves a current review file. Captures the coverage
accounting we care about -- modes/prngs/seed-range actually enumerated,
keys tried vs planned with explicit percent, throughput, elapsed, ETA,
errors -- plus a RESULT block and an explicit HONEST SCOPE statement that
the null applies only to the enumerated slice (not other seeds, PRNG
families, non-PRNG sources, or constructions the dict-hit metric is blind
to). _scan_near_misses() surfaces the strongest sub-threshold entries
across shards so 'how null was it' is visible rather than a bare zero.

New flag --summary-every N (0 = only at clean exit). Phase 9 selftest
covers both the clean-null and has-entries paths; full suite 9/9.
Verified end-to-end through main() on a live 200-seed run: params,
results, and run_summary.txt all produced.
---
 eyestat/eyestat_runner.py   | 208 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 eyestat/eyestat_selftest.py |  60 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 268 insertions(+)

diff --git a/eyestat/eyestat_runner.py b/eyestat/eyestat_runner.py
